    {
      "post_id": "80917",
      "author_handle": "mummyflynn",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 17 years 6 months ago",
      "body": "Hi\nI'm having real trouble making enough milk for my baby. I only seem to be making a couple of oz from each and I really wanted to avoid formula. I was hoping there might be someone close to Retford that might have a little spare to either give me or sell me?",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-8574/#80917",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/078da8f3feeb9aaf31b6.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-8574/",
      "role": "original_post",
      "original_post_id": "80917"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "80934",
      "author_handle": "soup",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 17 years 6 months ago",
      "body": "go to Holland and Barret and but some fenugreek and start taking 3 capsules 3 times a day to boost your supply\nalso feed often - take a nursing holiday where you spend the day in bed feeding and watching films - the more you feed the more you will make\n2 cups of fennel tea a day can help with your let down\nalso some people who have plenty of milk to feed baby can not express a great deal of milk out - dont judge your milk supply by your expressed amounts\nif your baby weight is an issue go to the doctor and ask to be prescribed domperidone - its an indigestion tablet that increases milk supply - i had to do this and without it i would never of been able to breastfeed how i am now\ndont give up - its worth fighting for",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-8574/#80934",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/078da8f3feeb9aaf31b6.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-8574/",
      "role": "response",
      "original_post_id": "80917"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "80939",
      "author_handle": "kristag",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 17 years 6 months ago",
      "body": "I agree with Soup. I was also worried at first that Sophie wasn't getting enough as I often seemed to only be able to express 2oz and wondered if she was ok?  She grew just fine and I ensured that my own fluid intake was good and also that I was taking time to eat myself (which wasn't always easy or top of my list!).\nIf you're really struggling, seek out a breastfeeding counsellor at your local NCT or hospital.\nDon't give up hun.  It's really worth it to carry on  😘",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-8574/#80939",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/078da8f3feeb9aaf31b6.html",
